{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:47:10Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 26, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "All 12 tests pass (8 existing + 4 new). The warnings are pre-existing environment issues unrelated to this change.\n\n## Backend implementation complete \u2014 Taiga #3\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 added `update_title(task_id, title) -> Optional[Task]`, mirroring `set_done`'s found-or-`None` pattern.\n- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 added `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}` route, reusing `TaskIn` for body validation, 404 on missing id, mirroring `complete_task`.\n- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 added 4 tests: title update succeeds, `done`/`id` are untouched by a title update, missing task is 404, empty title is 422 and doesn't mutate the stored title.\n\n**Verified:** `python3 -m pytest -q` in `backend/` \u2192 12 passed (8 existing + 4 new).\n\n**Scope note:** stayed strictly in `backend/` per the spec's split. Frontend (`api.js`, `TaskList.jsx`, `App.jsx`, `App.css`, e2e tests) is out of my scope \u2014 not touched.\n\nNo deviations from `docs/spec.md`/`docs/design.md`: endpoint shape (`PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}`), validation reuse (`TaskIn`), and 404 pattern all match what was specified.===OUTPUT2===\nGood \u2014 confirms exactly the expected files changed within my scope (`api.js`, `App.jsx`, `App.css`, `TaskList.jsx`, `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`), plus backend files already modified by the other agent.\n\nImplementation complete. Summary of the frontend work:\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 added `updateTask(id, title)` calling `PATCH /api/tasks/:id`, alongside `completeTask`/`deleteTask`.\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 added a `TaskRow` subcomponent with per-row `isEditing`/`draft`/`showError` state: Edit button, inline edit form (input + Save/Cancel), disabled-Save + inline `.field-error` for empty/whitespace titles, Escape-to-cancel, autofocus+select on entering edit mode.\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 wired `onUpdate` to `TaskList`; changed `run()` to return `true`/`false` on success/failure (previously returned nothing) so `TaskRow` can tell whether to close edit mode.\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 added `.task-edit`, `.task-title-input`, `.field-error` styles per the design doc, reusing existing colors/spacing.\n- `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py` \u2014 8 new tests covering prefill, save, cancel (no backend call), disabled Save on empty, Enter-key rejection of empty/whitespace titles, and `done` state independence.\n\n**One deviation from the design doc, found during testing:** the design assumed pressing Enter always fires the form's `onSubmit` even with a disabled Save button. That's false in Chromium \u2014 a disabled single submit button blocks native implicit-submit-on-Enter, so the empty-title error never appeared. Fixed by handling Enter explicitly in `TaskRow`'s `onKeyDown` (`e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py:203`/`212` initially failed, now pass \u2014 see `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`).\n\n**Verification run this session:** `npm run build` (passes), full e2e suite `python3 -m pytest e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py -q` (28 passed). `npm run lint` (oxlint) could not be run \u2014 the sandbox blocked it pending approval I couldn't obtain non-interactively; flagging this gap rather than claiming it passed.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Mg4xKgtwC9vbq51xV3Yi7n", "session_id": "b32343ef-8914-468a-8d74-824b5074f2c5"}}
