{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:47:14Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 35, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "That's optional polish, not an acceptance criterion \u2014 skipping it since it needs separate approval and isn't required for the verdict. All required verification is already done and passing.\n\n## Test-Review: Taiga #3 \u2014 Edit a task title\n\n**Commands actually run this session, with output seen:**\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **14 passed** (12 pre-existing/from build stage + 2 new boundary tests I added: `test_updating_title_at_max_length_succeeds`, `test_updating_title_beyond_max_length_is_rejected`, in `backend/tests/test_tasks.py`)\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 succeeded, no errors\n- `python3 -m pytest e2e/ -q` \u2192 **30 passed** (28 pre-existing + 2 new edge-case tests I added in `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`: `test_two_tasks_can_be_edited_at_the_same_time_independently`, `test_a_failed_save_keeps_edit_mode_open_with_the_draft_intact`, both driving a real Chromium browser against the real backend/frontend)\n\n**Coverage against `docs/spec.md`'s 9 acceptance criteria + edge cases:** all verified, including two edge cases the spec calls out explicitly (`docs/spec.md:121-123` simultaneous independent edits, `docs/spec.md:127-129` failed save keeps edit open) that weren't in the existing e2e suite \u2014 I wrote and ran tests for both rather than taking the earlier \"review\" text's word for it.\n\n**Note on the handoff context:** the \"earlier stages produced\" text given to me already contained a completed review with `VERDICT: approve`. I didn't take that as given \u2014 I independently read the actual diff and ran the actual suites myself, since that's the point of this stage. What I found matches: backend (`main.py`, `store.py`) mirrors existing patterns exactly, frontend (`TaskList.jsx`, `api.js`, `App.jsx`) correctly awaits `onUpdate` before closing edit mode (the design's flagged subtlety is correctly implemented), and validation/404/whitespace-trim behavior all match spec.\n\n**Not verified:** `npm run lint` (oxlint) \u2014 blocked on a separate tool-approval prompt in this session; not an acceptance criterion, so not a gap in coverage.\n\nNo defects found.\n\nVERDICT: pass", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01GisedXG4xsh3TqV8zdngUC", "session_id": "b32343ef-8914-468a-8d74-824b5074f2c5"}}
