{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:48:58Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 123, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "17:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T10:13:40Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 17, \"kind\": \"message\", \"text\": \"I'll start by examining the diff against the main branch to review the frontend work for editing task titles (Taiga #2).\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"text\", \"session_id\": \"e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c\"}}\n58:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T10:13:59Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 58, \"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"text\": \"1\\t# Spec: Edit a task title\\n2\\t\\n3\\tTaiga #2\\n4\\t\\n5\\t## Triage\\n6\\t\\n7\\t**Feature** \\u2014 net-new capability, no existing behaviour changes. Single\\n8\\tcohesive cycle: one new backend route plus the frontend UI to drive it. Does\\n9\\tnot span enough architectural layers to warrant splitting (compare: Taiga #1\\n10\\twas frontend-only; this one adds one backend route + one store method + one\\n11\\tcomponent's edit state \\u2014 normal size for one cycle).\\n12\\t\\n13\\t## Goal\\n14\\t\\n15\\tLet someone fix a mistyped task title in place, without deleting and\\n16\\tre-creating the task.\\n17\\t\\n18\\t## Acceptance criteria\\n19\\t\\n20\\t1. **Enter edit mode.** Given a task in the list, when the user activates\\n21\\t   editing on it, then the title is replaced with an editable input\\n22\\t   pre-filled with the task's current title.\\n23\\t2. **Save a valid edit.** Given a task in edit mode, when the user submits a\\n24\\t   new title that is non-empty after trimming, then the task's title is\\n25\\t   updated, the change is persisted (still present after a page reload), and\\n26\\t   edit mode closes showing the new title.\\n27\\t3. **Cancel discards changes.** Given a task in edit mode with a modified\\n28\\t   draft, when the user cancels, then the title reverts to its original\\n29\\t   value, no save request is sent, and edit mode closes.\\n30\\t4. **Empty title is rejected, not saved.** Given a task in edit mode, when\\n31\\t   the user submits a title that is empty or whitespace-only, then the save\\n32\\t   is rejected: the task's title is unchanged (never blanked), the user gets\\n33\\t   visible feedback that the title can't be empty, and they remain able to\\n34\\t   correct it without having lost their place.\\n35\\t5. **Oversized title is rejected.** Given a task in edit mode, when the user\\n36\\t   submits a title over 200 characters (the existing `TaskIn` limit used for\\n37\\t   create), then the save is rejected the same way create rejects it today,\\n38\\t   and the task's title is unchanged.\\n39\\t6. **Backend: successful update.** Given an existing task, when\\n40\\t   `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}` is called with `{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<1-200 chars>\\\"}`, then\\n41\\t   it returns `200` with the updated `Task`, and a subsequent `GET\\n42\\t   /api/tasks` reflects the new title.\\n43\\t7. **Backend: missing task.** Given no task with that id, when `PATCH\\n44\\t   /api/tasks/{id}` is called, then it returns `404`.\\n45\\t8. **Backend: empty title.** Given an existing task, when `PATCH\\n46\\t   /api/tasks/{id}` is called with `{\\\"title\\\": \\\"\\\"}`, then it returns `422`\\n47\\t   and the stored title is unchanged.\\n48\\t\\n49\\t## Non-goals\\n50\\t\\n51\\t- No edit history or undo beyond the in-progress cancel.\\n52\\t- No multi-field bulk edit, no editing multiple tasks' titles at once.\\n53\\t- No new concurrency/conflict resolution beyond what already exists \\u2014 a save\\n54\\t  against a task deleted by someone else surfaces as a `404` through the\\n55\\t  existing error banner (`App.jsx`'s `run()` \\u2192 `setError`), same as\\n56\\t  completing or deleting an already-gone task does today.\\n57\\t- No character counter or other new max-length UI beyond reusing the\\n58\\t  existing 200-char backend validation.\\n59\\t\\n60\\t## Affected areas\\n61\\t\\n62\\t- `backend/app/main.py` \\u2014 add `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}` route (mirrors\\n63\\t  the existing `POST /api/tasks/{task_id}/done` route shape at lines 32-37).\\n64\\t- `backend/app/store.py` \\u2014 add `TaskStore.set_title(task_id, title)`,\\n65\\t  mirroring `set_done` (lines 30-35).\\n66\\t- `backend/app/models.py` \\u2014 no change; the new route reuses `TaskIn`\\n67\\t  (line 5-6) for its request body, same validation as create.\\n68\\t- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \\u2014 add tests for the new route, following the\\n69\\t  existing `client` fixture pattern (success, 404, 422 empty title).\\n70\\t- `frontend/src/api.js` \\u2014 add `updateTask(id, title)` issuing a `PATCH`,\\n71\\t  next to `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (lines 20-21).\\n72\\t- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \\u2014 add per-task edit-mode state and\\n73\\t  the editable-input UI (currently renders `task-title` as plain text at\\n74\\t  line 15).\\n75\\t- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \\u2014 add an `onEdit` handler wired through the\\n76\\t  existing `run()` helper (lines 33-40), same pattern as `onComplete` /\\n77\\t  `onDelete` (lines 54-55).\\n78\\t- `frontend/src/App.css` \\u2014 styles for the edit input and its save/cancel\\n79\\t  controls, extending the existing `.task` rules (lines 30-35).\\n80\\t\\n81\\tExact trigger affordance, save/cancel control placement, and any\\n82\\tkeyboard-shortcut behavior (e.g. Enter/Escape) beyond the input's minimum\\n83\\tsave/cancel actions are the ux-designer's call, not fixed here.\\n84\\t\\n85\\t## Edge cases\\n86\\t\\n87\\t- Empty title submitted \\u2192 rejected, task unchanged (AC4).\\n88\\t- Whitespace-only title (`\\\"   \\\"`) \\u2192 trimmed before validation, treated the\\n89\\t  same as empty (AC4). Trimming happens client-side before the request is\\n90\\t  sent, same as `AddTask.jsx` already does for creation (line 8).\\n91\\t- Cancel with a modified draft \\u2192 reverts, no request sent (AC3).\\n92\\t- Save with the draft identical to the original title \\u2192 treated as a normal\\n93\\t  save (a `PATCH` is still sent); not special-cased, since it's harmless and\\n94\\t  idempotent in this in-memory store.\\n95\\t- Title over 200 characters \\u2192 rejected by existing `TaskIn` validation\\n96\\t  (AC5), surfaced to the user rather than failing silently.\\n97\\t- Task deleted by another client while being edited \\u2192 save fails with `404`,\\n98\\t  surfaced through the existing error banner (see Non-goals).\\n99\\t- Editing a task that is already marked `done` \\u2192 allowed; nothing in the\\n100\\t  request restricts editing to open tasks only (see Open Questions).\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"user\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_014aBiQNdN51MVAQQ8Qd5wL4\", \"session_id\": \"e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c\"}}\n189:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T10:15:48Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 189, \"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"text\": \"# Design: Edit a task title\\n\\nTaiga #2 \\u00b7 consumes `docs/spec.md`\\n\\n## Conventions established (before designing anything)\\n\\n- No component library, no icon set, no design tokens file \\u2014 plain CSS in\\n  `frontend/src/App.css`, function components, hooks only.\\n- Existing button style is a single neutral style (`button { border, white\\n  bg, radius 5px }`) with no primary/secondary visual hierarchy \\u2014 Done and\\n  Delete look the same. Nothing today distinguishes \\\"safe\\\" vs \\\"destructive\\\"\\n  by color.\\n- Existing form pattern is `AddTask.jsx`: a `<form onSubmit>` wrapping an\\n  `<input>` + submit `<button>`, client-side `.trim()` check before calling\\n  the handler, `aria-label` on the input.\\n- Existing per-row actions (`TaskList.jsx`) are plain-text buttons with an\\n  `aria-label` that includes the task's title (`` `Complete ${task.title}` ``)\\n  for screen-reader disambiguation between rows.\\n- Existing error surface is a single global banner in `App.jsx` \\u2014\\n  `<p className=\\\"error\\\" role=\\\"alert\\\">` \\u2014 fed by `run()`'s catch block.\\n- Existing color tokens in use: text `#16191c`, border `#ccd2d6`, error text\\n  `#a3271d` on error bg `#fbe9e7`, muted `#6b7780`, card bg `#fff`, page bg\\n  `#f6f7f8`.\\n\\n**Decision: introduce no new component, no new color, no new button style.**\\nEverything below extends `TaskList.jsx` and `App.css` in place, per the\\nspec's affected areas.\\n\\n## Interaction model\\n\\n`TaskList` owns edit state locally (per spec: \\\"per-task edit-mode state\\\"):\\n\\n```js\\nconst [editingId, setEditingId] = useState(null)\\nconst [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\\nconst [validationError, setValidationError] = useState(null)\\n```\\n\\n- **Enter edit mode** \\u2014 click a task's `Edit` button \\u2192\\n  `setEditingId(task.id); setDraft(task.title); setValidationError(null)`.\\n  The input autofocuses (`autoFocus` \\u2014 safe here since it only fires on a\\n  direct user click, not on page load).\\n- **Opening edit on a different task** \\u2014 clicking `Edit` elsewhere just calls\\n  `startEdit` again; `editingId`/`draft` are overwritten, so the previous\\n  row's unsaved draft is silently discarded. This *is* the resolution to the\\n  spec's open question 2 (only one task edits at a time) \\u2014 no confirmation\\n  dialog, per the spec's stated default.\\n- **Cancel** \\u2014 `Cancel` button, or `Escape` in the input \\u2192\\n  `setEditingId(null); setValidationError(null)`. No request sent. The row\\n  re-renders from `tasks` (untouched), so the original title reappears with\\n  no extra revert logic needed.\\n- **Save, empty/whitespace draft (AC4)** \\u2014 submit handler trims the draft\\n  first, same as `AddTask.jsx` line 8. If empty, **block before calling\\n  `onEdit`**: `setValidationError(\\\"Title can't be empty.\\\")`, keep\\n  `editingId` set, return. No request is sent, focus stays in the input\\n  (it never lost focus), the draft the user typed is preserved so they can\\n  fix it in place.\\n- **Save, valid draft (AC2)** \\u2014 trimmed non-empty value \\u2192 close edit mode\\n  immediately (`setEditingId(null)`), call `onEdit(task.id, trimmed)`. This\\n  is optimistic: the row briefly shows the old title until `App.jsx`'s\\n  `run()` \\u2192 `refresh()` completes, then shows the new one. No new\\n  loading-state UI is introduced for this, matching Complete/Delete, which\\n  have the same brief-old-value-until-refresh gap today.\\n- **Save, oversized draft (AC5)** \\u2014 no client-side length check is added\\n  (spec non-goal). An over-200-char draft is *not* caught by the empty\\n  check, so it takes the same path as a valid save: edit mode closes\\n  optimistically, the request goes out, the backend 422s, and the existing\\n  global banner in `App.jsx` shows it \\u2014 identical to how `AddTask` handles\\n  an oversized create today. This means AC5, unlike AC4, does *not* keep\\n  edit mode open on rejection \\u2014 that asymmetry is intentional: the spec says\\n  AC5 should be rejected \\\"the same way create rejects it today,\\\" and create\\n  has no such behavior either. If this asymmetry is undesirable, the fix is\\n  a client-side length guard, which is explicitly out of scope (non-goal:\\n  \\\"No character counter or other new max-length UI\\\").\\n- **Click elsewhere on the page while editing** \\u2014 no effect. Edit mode is\\n  not exited by blur/click-outside; only explicit Cancel, Escape, Save, or\\n  switching to another row's Edit closes it. (Not specified by the spec;\\n  chosen because silent data loss on an accidental click is worse than\\n  requiring an explicit action.)\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"user\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01XtMdL6RnZNdJBDRuAEsfug\", \"session_id\": \"e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c\"}}\n213:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T10:16:24Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 213, \"kind\": \"message\", \"text\": \"## Review \\u2014 Taiga #2: Edit a task title\\n\\n**Verified:** `python3 -m pytest -q` \\u2192 11 passed (backend). `npm run build` \\u2192 clean. Read the full diff, `docs/spec.md`, and `docs/design.md` against it.\\n\\n\\u26a0\\ufe0f **Disclosure, not a finding:** while testing the 422 response shape I created a scratch file `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` to inspect FastAPI's validation error body. It's untracked (`git status` confirms), and my sandbox permissions block `rm`/`git clean` on this session, so it's still sitting in the working tree. **Please delete `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` before committing** \\u2014 it is not part of the developer's work.\\n\\n### Will block\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Will comment\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Worth considering\\n\\n1. **`frontend/src/api.js:8-11` (`request()`, unchanged by this diff) \\u2014 oversized-title rejection (AC5) will render as `[object Object]`, not readable text.** FastAPI's 422 body puts `detail` as a *list* of validation-error objects, not a string (confirmed by hitting `PATCH` with a 201-char title: `{'detail': [{'type': 'string_too_long', ...}]}`). `request()` does `detail?.detail || ...` and throws `new Error(detail.detail)`, so `error.message` stringifies the array as `[object Object]` in the global banner. This is pre-existing (same path `AddTask` create already uses, `request()` itself is untouched by this diff), and `docs/design.md:64-71` explicitly reasons through this and accepts the asymmetry as intentional parity with create's existing behavior \\u2014 so it's correctly out of scope for this cycle. Flagging only because AC5 says \\\"surfaced to the user,\\\" and today that surfacing is unreadable; worth a follow-up ticket on `request()`'s error formatting, not a blocker here.\\n2. **No automated frontend test was added** for the new edit-mode UI (cancel/empty-rejection/save flows). Per the story stage's own note, `frontend/package.json` has no test framework installed despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test` \\u2014 a pre-existing infra gap, not something this feature should fix solo, but it means AC1-5 (all frontend-only) are currently verified only by manual/design review, not a test suite. Worth a separate ticket to stand up frontend testing infra.\\n\\n### Spec/design conformance check (for the record)\\n\\nAll 8 ACs trace cleanly to the diff: AC1 (`startEdit`), AC2 (optimistic close + `run()`\\u2192refresh), AC3 (`cancelEdit`, Escape handler), AC4 (client-side trim-guard, `role=\\\"alert\\\"`, edit mode stays open), AC5 (deliberately unguarded, per non-goal), AC6-8 (`backend/tests/test_tasks.py:42-60`, all passing). Both open questions from the spec (done tasks stay editable; single-task edit mode) are implemented as their stated defaults. No new component/color/pattern introduced beyond what `docs/design.md` scoped \\u2014 reuses `AddTask`'s form/trim pattern and the existing error-banner path faithfully.\\n\\nVERDICT: approve-with-followups\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"text\", \"session_id\": \"e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c\"}}\n214:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T10:16:24Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 214, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"## Review \\u2014 Taiga #2: Edit a task title\\n\\n**Verified:** `python3 -m pytest -q` \\u2192 11 passed (backend). `npm run build` \\u2192 clean. Read the full diff, `docs/spec.md`, and `docs/design.md` against it.\\n\\n\\u26a0\\ufe0f **Disclosure, not a finding:** while testing the 422 response shape I created a scratch file `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` to inspect FastAPI's validation error body. It's untracked (`git status` confirms), and my sandbox permissions block `rm`/`git clean` on this session, so it's still sitting in the working tree. **Please delete `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` before committing** \\u2014 it is not part of the developer's work.\\n\\n### Will block\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Will comment\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Worth considering\\n\\n1. **`frontend/src/api.js:8-11` (`request()`, unchanged by this diff) \\u2014 oversized-title rejection (AC5) will render as `[object Object]`, not readable text.** FastAPI's 422 body puts `detail` as a *list* of validation-error objects, not a string (confirmed by hitting `PATCH` with a 201-char title: `{'detail': [{'type': 'string_too_long', ...}]}`). `request()` does `detail?.detail || ...` and throws `new Error(detail.detail)`, so `error.message` stringifies the array as `[object Object]` in the global banner. This is pre-existing (same path `AddTask` create already uses, `request()` itself is untouched by this diff), and `docs/design.md:64-71` explicitly reasons through this and accepts the asymmetry as intentional parity with create's existing behavior \\u2014 so it's correctly out of scope for this cycle. Flagging only because AC5 says \\\"surfaced to the user,\\\" and today that surfacing is unreadable; worth a follow-up ticket on `request()`'s error formatting, not a blocker here.\\n2. **No automated frontend test was added** for the new edit-mode UI (cancel/empty-rejection/save flows). Per the story stage's own note, `frontend/package.json` has no test framework installed despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test` \\u2014 a pre-existing infra gap, not something this feature should fix solo, but it means AC1-5 (all frontend-only) are currently verified only by manual/design review, not a test suite. Worth a separate ticket to stand up frontend testing infra.\\n\\n### Spec/design conformance check (for the record)\\n\\nAll 8 ACs trace cleanly to the diff: AC1 (`startEdit`), AC2 (optimistic close + `run()`\\u2192refresh), AC3 (`cancelEdit`, Escape handler), AC4 (client-side trim-guard, `role=\\\"alert\\\"`, edit mode stays open), AC5 (deliberately unguarded, per non-goal), AC6-8 (`backend/tests/test_tasks.py:42-60`, all passing). Both open questions from the spec (done tasks stay editable; single-task edit mode) are implemented as their stated defaults. No new component/color/pattern introduced beyond what `docs/design.md` scoped \\u2014 reuses `AddTask`'s form/trim pattern and the existing error-banner path faithfully.\\n\\nVERDICT: approve-with-followups\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"result\", \"subtype\": \"success\", \"session_id\": \"e55e5722-705b-4388-9b58-e93f4aa20d7c\", \"is_error\": false, \"total_cost_usd\": 1.0768340999999997}}\n364:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T10:44:27Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 150, \"kind\": \"message\", \"text\": \"## Review: Taiga #3 \\u2014 Edit a task title\\n\\n**Verified, not just read:**\\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \\u2192 12/12 passed\\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \\u2192 succeeds\\n- `python3 -m pytest e2e/ -q` \\u2192 28/28 passed (including all 9 new edit-title scenarios: prefill, save, save-closes-edit, cancel-reverts-no-backend-call, disabled-Save-on-empty, Enter-rejects-empty, Enter-rejects-whitespace, done-state-preserved)\\n\\nNote: the handoff text claimed the developer \\\"stayed strictly in backend/... frontend is out of my scope \\u2014 not touched,\\\" but the actual diff includes substantial frontend changes (`TaskList.jsx`, `api.js`, `App.jsx`, `App.css`, e2e tests). I disregarded that claim and reviewed/tested the code as it actually stands rather than as reported \\u2014 flagging this only so the orchestrator is aware the stage report doesn't match the diff, though the code itself is sound.\\n\\n**Will block:** none.\\n\\n**Will comment:** none.\\n\\n**Worth considering:**\\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`'s `onKeyDown` Enter handler is a deliberate, commented deviation from `docs/design.md`'s sketch (which only wired Escape). It's correct \\u2014 a disabled Save button blocks native implicit form-submission-on-Enter, so this is required to make AC5 (whitespace-only via Enter) actually surface the inline error \\u2014 and it's proven by the passing e2e tests. Flagging only as a documented deviation, not a defect.\\n- The server-side whitespace-only quirk (`TaskIn`'s `min_length=1` counts raw characters, so `\\\"   \\\"` would pass Pydantic on a direct API call) is *not* fixed by this PR \\u2014 but that's an explicit, spec-documented non-goal (`docs/spec.md:63-68`), consistent with the same pre-existing quirk on `create`, and the UI-facing path is fully guarded client-side (trimmed before submit) and tested server-side for the true-empty case. Not a gap in this feature's actual acceptance criteria.\\n\\nAll 9 acceptance criteria in `docs/spec.md` are covered by tests and pass. Backend mirrors `set_done`'s exact pattern; frontend reuses `.add-task`'s existing styles and `AddTask`'s trim-guard idiom. No scope creep, no unjustified surface added.\\n\\nVERDICT: approve\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"text\", \"session_id\": \"e57fba9e-0cb2-4bf7-b0c9-98e040eea1a9\"}}\n365:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T10:44:27Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 151, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"## Review: Taiga #3 \\u2014 Edit a task title\\n\\n**Verified, not just read:**\\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \\u2192 12/12 passed\\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \\u2192 succeeds\\n- `python3 -m pytest e2e/ -q` \\u2192 28/28 passed (including all 9 new edit-title scenarios: prefill, save, save-closes-edit, cancel-reverts-no-backend-call, disabled-Save-on-empty, Enter-rejects-empty, Enter-rejects-whitespace, done-state-preserved)\\n\\nNote: the handoff text claimed the developer \\\"stayed strictly in backend/... frontend is out of my scope \\u2014 not touched,\\\" but the actual diff includes substantial frontend changes (`TaskList.jsx`, `api.js`, `App.jsx`, `App.css`, e2e tests). I disregarded that claim and reviewed/tested the code as it actually stands rather than as reported \\u2014 flagging this only so the orchestrator is aware the stage report doesn't match the diff, though the code itself is sound.\\n\\n**Will block:** none.\\n\\n**Will comment:** none.\\n\\n**Worth considering:**\\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`'s `onKeyDown` Enter handler is a deliberate, commented deviation from `docs/design.md`'s sketch (which only wired Escape). It's correct \\u2014 a disabled Save button blocks native implicit form-submission-on-Enter, so this is required to make AC5 (whitespace-only via Enter) actually surface the inline error \\u2014 and it's proven by the passing e2e tests. Flagging only as a documented deviation, not a defect.\\n- The server-side whitespace-only quirk (`TaskIn`'s `min_length=1` counts raw characters, so `\\\"   \\\"` would pass Pydantic on a direct API call) is *not* fixed by this PR \\u2014 but that's an explicit, spec-documented non-goal (`docs/spec.md:63-68`), consistent with the same pre-existing quirk on `create`, and the UI-facing path is fully guarded client-side (trimmed before submit) and tested server-side for the true-empty case. Not a gap in this feature's actual acceptance criteria.\\n\\nAll 9 acceptance criteria in `docs/spec.md` are covered by tests and pass. Backend mirrors `set_done`'s exact pattern; frontend reuses `.add-task`'s existing styles and `AddTask`'s trim-guard idiom. No scope creep, no unjustified surface added.\\n\\nVERDICT: approve\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"result\", \"subtype\": \"success\", \"session_id\": \"e57fba9e-0cb2-4bf7-b0c9-98e040eea1a9\", \"is_error\": false, \"total_cost_usd\": 0.8621549999999999}}", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Mtx9VSefC6L2kQ7vFs4Y6v", "session_id": "b32343ef-8914-468a-8d74-824b5074f2c5"}}
