{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:51:38Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 265, "kind": "message", "text": "This confirms it: round 2 actually ran twice. The first pass (Taiga #2) got through story\u2192design\u2192build\u2192review, but the reviewer created a scratch file (`backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py`) to inspect a FastAPI error shape, then couldn't clean it up \u2014 `rm` and `git clean` were both blocked by sandbox permissions. That dirty untracked file evidently forced the whole cycle to be abandoned and restarted from scratch as Taiga #3, which is the only version that made it into the merge commit. That's a full extra story\u2192design\u2192build\u2192review pass wasted \u2014 the single biggest cost in this round's evidence.\n\nLet me check the exact scratch-file incident once more and then make the fix.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "b32343ef-8914-468a-8d74-824b5074f2c5"}}
